{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdtvDXeMzxDyeiMteotPd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Diagnostic Plan\n\n1. **Re-invoke `status.get_health()` immediately in this same session** (warm retry).\n   - This is a read-only, safe, idempotent call — explicitly retriable per ladder 3.\n   - A cold-start timeout on first invocation in a fresh session is a known, session-scoped confound.\n   - The retry costs one call and directly settles whether the first failure was cold-start latency or a genuine capability gap.\n\n2. **Classify the outcome:**\n   - **If the warm call returns promptly with valid health data:** Record the first timeout as cold-start latency (log as incident if tracking, but it does not count against the service's capability record). The service is **provisionally usable** for routing — but only provisionally. Do not yet route load-bearing work; confirm reachability with a differential before committing risk-sensitive decisions (ladder 1: call a different cheap endpoint on the same path, or verify across a second session).\n   - **If the warm call still times out or returns an explicit error (not \"cold\"):** Escalate to ladder 1 (single-endpoint failure). Verify the key/gateway with a different cheap call; rule out parsing on your side with a raw re-probe. The service is **UNRESOLVED or DOWN** — do not route work until differential diagnosis completes.\n\n3. **Record capability status:** \n   - Do not record this service as DOWN yet. The first timeout alone, without a warm retry outcome, is insufficient evidence (ladder 3 explicitly forbids recording a cold-start timeout as proof of death).\n   - Pending the warm retry result, mark status as **UNKNOWN**."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1832,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_token